[?2004l[?2004h> # hookrelay
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Delivers signed webhooks to customer endpoints from a persistent SQLite outbox.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h>     python -m hookrelay enqueue EVENT_ID URL body.json
[?2004l[?2004h>     python -m hookrelay dispatch [--limit N]
[?2004l[?2004h>     python -m hookrelay status
[?2004l[?2004h>     python -m hookrelay dlq
[?2004l[?2004h>     python -m hookrelay replay ID
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Transient failures stay pending and are retried with deterministic exponential
[?2004l[?2004h> backoff (starting at about 30 seconds, capped at one hour). Retry-After seconds
[?2004l[?2004h> are honored up to that cap. Run `dispatch` periodically to process due deliveries;
[?2004l[?2004h> it reports JSON counts for `delivered`, `retried`, and `dead`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Permanent failures and retryable failures on the eighth attempt are dead-lettered.
[?2004l[?2004h> `dlq` prints the dead-letter history as a JSON array, oldest first. `replay ID`
[?2004l[?2004h> resets a dead delivery's attempts and makes it due immediately, preserving its
[?2004l[?2004h> payload and dead-letter history. It prints `{"replayed": true}` and exits 0 on
[?2004l[?2004h> success, or `{"replayed": false}` and exits 1 if the ID is missing or not dead.
[?2004l[?2004h> Neither DLQ command requires the signing key.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> See [docs/RETRIES.md](docs/RETRIES.md) for the retry policy and Python API.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> CI: `scripts/ci.sh` (pytest + branch-coverage gate, see `pyproject.toml`).
